{"name":"Lemur","hex":"#695f4f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Lemur","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Lemuridae – ring-tailed lemur."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Lemur"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lemur","blocks":[{"text":"Lemurs are wet-nosed primates of the superfamily Lemuroidea, divided into eight families and consisting of 15 genera and around 100 extant species. They are endemic to the island of Madagascar. Most existing lemurs are small, with a pointed snout, large eyes, and a long tail. They usually live in trees and are active at night. Lemurs share resemblance with other primates, but evolved independently from monkeys and apes. Due to Madagascar's highly seasonal climate, lemur evolution has produced a level of species diversity rivaling that of any other primate group."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Coquerel%27s_sifaka_%28Propithecus_coquereli%29.jpg/330px-Coquerel%27s_sifaka_%28Propithecus_coquereli%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemur","wikidata":"Q1192405"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Babakotia_radofilai.jpg/500px-Babakotia_radofilai.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Babakotia_radofilai.jpg/1280px-Babakotia_radofilai.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Babakotia_radofilai.jpg/500px-Babakotia_radofilai.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A life restoration of Babakotia radofilai, a sloth lemur that became extinct less than two thousand years ago","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABabakotia_radofilai.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thum